  <div class="container">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">The rules for using our tools and learning topics. Please read them before you use the website.<br>
    <strong>Last updated: 27 October 2026</strong></p>

    <!-- Quick Glance -->
    <div class="glance">
      <div class="glance-item">
        <b>Official domain</b>
        <span>New tools and updates are published only at pooretools.win.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="glance-item">
        <b>Use at your own risk</b>
        <span>Tools and content are provided “as is”, with no guarantee of results.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="glance-item">
        <b>Your files, your duty</b>
        <span>Keep backups and avoid entering sensitive information.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="glance-item">
        <b>Use it fairly</b>
        <span>No illegal use, abuse, or use without permission.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="terms-grid">

      <!-- 01 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s1">
        <h2><span>01</span> Acceptance of These Terms</h2>
        <p>By visiting or using PooreTools (the “Website”), including its tools, calculators, converters, utilities, learning topics, tutorials, and other resources (together, the “Services”), you agree to these Terms of Use. You also agree to our <a href="privacy.html">Privacy Policy &amp; Disclaimer</a>, which is part of these Terms.</p>
        <p>If you do not agree, please do not use the Services. Using the Services means you accept these Terms.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 02 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s2">
        <h2><span>02</span> Official Domains &amp; Transition</h2>
        <p>The official website of PooreTools is <a href="https://pooretools.win">pooretools.win</a>. This is the only place where new tools, new pages, and updates to existing tools are published.</p>
        <p>PooreTools and our earlier site, <a href="https://pooreyoutuber.github.io/">pooreyoutuber.github.io</a>, are both run by the same developer. We are not shutting the older site down, and it will stay online. However, no new tools or updates will be added there from now on. Tools on the older site have been rebuilt, updated, and in several cases expanded on PooreTools, and any new sections will appear only on PooreTools.</p>
        <p>The main purpose of both sites is to provide useful tools to people for free.</p>
        <p>If you find a PooreTools page on any other domain, a copy, or a page claiming to be PooreTools, it is not published by us. Please verify the address before entering information or relying on the content.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 03 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s3">
        <h2><span>03</span> About the Services</h2>
        <p>PooreTools is an independent website that offers online tools and learning topics across many subjects. Some Services may be new, experimental, or still being improved.</p>
        <p>We may add, change, pause, limit, or remove any tool, topic, feature, or part of the Website at any time, with or without notice, and without any duty to keep a Service available or to keep a particular result, file, or page.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 04 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s4">
        <h2><span>04</span> Who May Use the Services</h2>
        <p>You must be old enough to form a binding agreement under the law that applies to you. If you are a minor, you may use the Services only with the permission and supervision of a parent or guardian, who is responsible for your use and accepts these Terms on your behalf.</p>
        <p>You must not use the Services if the law prohibits you from doing so.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 05 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s5">
        <h2><span>05</span> Learning Content Is for General Information</h2>
        <p>Our topics, tutorials, examples, formulas, practice questions, and guides are for general learning and information only. They may contain mistakes, may be incomplete, and may become outdated as rules, standards, technology, and knowledge change.</p>
        <p>They are not official study material, not a substitute for qualified teaching, and not a guarantee of any exam result, job outcome, or other result. You must verify anything important with reliable, current, and official sources before relying on it.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 06 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s6">
        <h2><span>06</span> Tools and Their Results</h2>
        <p>Tools such as calculators, estimators, converters, generators, analysers, and editors give results based on what you enter and on how the tool is built. Results may be affected by rounding, assumptions, browser or device differences, outside services, or errors in the tool.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>All results are provided for general guidance and convenience only.</li>
          <li>Results are estimates and are not official, certified, or guaranteed to be correct.</li>
          <li>You must check important results yourself before making any decision, sending any document, or using any file or code.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You use every tool and every result at your own risk.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 07 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s7">
        <h2><span>07</span> Your Files, Inputs and Content</h2>
        <p>You are fully responsible for the files, text, images, data, and other material you enter, upload, or process using the Services (“Your Content”).</p>
        <ul>
          <li>You confirm that you own Your Content or have the right to use it, and that using it with the Services does not break any law or anyone’s rights.</li>
          <li>Please do not enter passwords, payment details, government ID numbers, confidential business information, or other sensitive data.</li>
          <li>Always keep your own backup. We do not promise that any file will be saved, kept, restored, or returned, and tools may fail, change a file, reduce its quality, or produce an unexpected result.</li>
          <li>You give us permission to process Your Content only as needed to operate the tool you chose. How information is handled is explained in our Privacy Policy, and not every tool works the same way.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not claim ownership of Your Content.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 08 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s8">
        <h2><span>08</span> Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>You agree to use the Services lawfully and fairly. You must not:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>break any law or regulation, or help anyone else to do so;</li>
          <li>process, upload, or create content that is illegal, harmful, abusive, harassing, hateful, defamatory, deceptive, or that infringes someone’s privacy, copyright, or other rights;</li>
          <li>use the Services for fraud, impersonation, scams, spam, or to mislead others, including forging documents or identities;</li>
          <li>use a tool on a file, person, system, or network without permission;</li>
          <li>upload malware, or try to damage, disrupt, overload, or gain unauthorised access to the Website, its servers, or other users’ data;</li>
          <li>use bots, scrapers, or automated methods to copy the Website or place heavy load on it, without our written permission;</li>
          <li>copy, resell, or redistribute our tools, content, or design as your own, or reverse engineer or extract the source code of any tool, except where the law clearly allows it; or</li>
          <li>bypass or interfere with any limit, security measure, or technical protection.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We may block, limit, or remove access, content, or features that we believe break these rules, without notice.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 09 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s9">
        <h2><span>09</span> Responsible and Authorised Technical Use</h2>
        <p>Some tutorials, code samples, and tools relate to networks, websites, code, or security. They are for lawful, authorised, educational, and defensive purposes only. You must have permission before testing or analysing anything that does not belong to you.</p>
        <p>You alone are responsible for how you use any code, command, script, or technique, and for any damage, loss, or legal consequence that follows. We do not guarantee that any tutorial or tool will work in your environment or give a safe or particular result.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 10 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s10">
        <h2><span>10</span> No Professional Advice</h2>
        <p>Nothing on the Website is legal, financial, tax, medical, accounting, investment, engineering, security, or other professional advice, and nothing creates a professional or advisory relationship with you. Please consult a qualified professional in the relevant field before acting on any information, and do not delay or ignore professional advice because of something you read here.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 11 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s11">
        <h2><span>11</span> Third-Party Services, Ads and Links</h2>
        <p>The Website may use or link to third-party services, advertising, analytics, embedded content, and external websites. We do not control them and are not responsible for their content, availability, security, products, or policies. Your use of any third-party service is at your own risk and under that service’s own terms.</p>
        <p>A link or mention does not mean that we endorse or guarantee that service.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 12 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s12">
        <h2><span>12</span> Our Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>The Website, including its design, text, topics, tutorials, tools, code, graphics, logo, and name, belongs to PooreTools or its licensors and is protected by intellectual property laws. Other trademarks and names belong to their owners.</p>
        <p>You may use the Services for your personal, non-commercial learning and productivity. Unless we give written permission, you must not copy, republish, sell, or build a competing product from our content or tools, or remove any notice of ownership. All rights not expressly given to you are reserved.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 13 -->
      <div class="term-card" id="s13">
        <h2><span>13</span> Feedback and Suggestions</h2>
        <p>If you send us feedback, ideas, or suggestions, you agree that we may use them freely, without payment, credit, or any duty to you. Please do not send anything you want to keep confidential.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 14 -->
